        style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;
mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none"><b
        style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span
          style="font-size:18.0pt;font-family:
          &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">IEEE Computing
          in Science &amp; Engineering<span
            style="mso-bidi-font-weight:bold"><o:p></o:p></span></span></b></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph;
mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:none"><b><span
          style="font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New
          Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="margin-bottom:17.0pt;mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:
      none;text-autospace:none"><b><span
          style="font-size:24.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New
          Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">Special
          Issue on Cloud Computing in Science &amp; Engineering<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="margin-bottom:17.0pt;mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:
      none;text-autospace:none"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><a
          href="http://www.computer.org/portal/web/computingnow/cise">http://www.computer.org/portal/web/computingnow/cise</a>
      </span><b><span style="font-size:24.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times
          New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="margin-bottom:13.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:
inter-ideograph;mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:
      none"><b><span style="font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New
          Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">Submissions
          due: November 04, 2012<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="margin-bottom:13.0pt;text-align:justify;text-justify:
inter-ideograph;mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:none;text-autospace:
      none"><b><span style="font-size:14.0pt;font-family:&quot;Times New
          Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">Estimated
          Publication date: July/August, 2013</span></b><span
        style="font-size:14.0pt;
        font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times
        New Roman&quot;">Cloud
        computing has emerged as a dominant paradigm that has been
        widely adopted by
        enterprises. Clouds provide on-demand access to computing
        utilities, an
        abstraction of unlimited computing resources, and support for
        on-demand scale
        up, scale down and scale out. Clouds are also rapidly joining
        more traditional
        computing platforms as viable platforms for scientific
        exploration and discovery,
        and education. As a result, understanding application
        formulations and usage
        modes that are meaningful in such a hybrid infrastructure, what
        are the
        fundamental conceptual and technological challenges, and how
        applications can
        effectively utilize it, is critical.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times
        New Roman&quot;"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times
        New Roman&quot;">The
        goal of this special issue of CiSE is to explore how Clouds
        platforms and
        abstractions, either by themselves or in combination with other
        platforms, can
        be effectively used to support real-world science and
        engineering applications.
      </span><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-weight:
        bold">Topics of interest include (but are not limited to)
        algorithmic and
        application formulations, programming models and systems,
        runtime systems and
        middleware, end-to-end application workflows and experiences
        with real
        applications. </span><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;
        mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times
        New Roman&quot;"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">Published
by
        the IEEE Computer Society, Computing in Science &amp;
        Engineering magazine
        features the latest computational science and engineering
        research in an
        accessible format, along with departments covering news and
        analysis, CSE in
        education, and emerging technologies. </span><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;
        mso-fareast-font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">We
        strongly encourage submissions that include multimedia, data,
        and community
        content, which will be featured on the IEEE Computer Society
        website along with
        the accepted papers.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><b><span
          style="font-family:&quot;Times New
          Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="margin-bottom:17.0pt;mso-pagination:none;mso-layout-grid-align:
      none;text-autospace:none"><span style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;
        mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">For more information please see
        <a class="moz-txt-link-freetext" href="http://www.computer.org/portal/web/computingnow/cscfp4">http://www.computer.org/portal/web/computingnow/cscfp4</a>
        <o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><b><span
          style="font-family:&quot;Times New
          Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">Questions?<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">Contact guest editors <b
          style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal">Manish Parashar, </b>Rutgers
        University (parashar
        at rutgers.edu) or <b>George K. Thiruvathukal, </b>Loyola
        University Chicago<span style="mso-bidi-font-weight:bold">&#8232;(gkt
          at cs.luc.edu).<b><o:p></o:p></b></span></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><b><span
          style="font-family:&quot;Times New
          Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><b><span
          style="font-family:&quot;Times New
          Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">Submission Guidelines<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">Authors are asked to submit
        high-quality original work that has neither appeared in nor is
        under
        consideration by other journals.&nbsp; All submissions will be
        peer-reviewed
        following standard journal practices. Manuscripts based on
        previously published
        conference papers must be extended substantially to include at
        least 30 percent
        new material. Manuscripts should be written in the active voice,
        should be no
        longer than 7,200 words (counting each standard figure and table
        as 250 words),
        and should follow the style and presentation guidelines of <i>CiSE
        </i>(see </span><a href="http://www.computer.org/cise/author"><b><span
            style="font-family:&quot;Times New
            Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">www.computer.org/cise/author</span></b></a><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"> for details).&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
    <p class="MsoNormal"
      style="text-align:justify;text-justify:inter-ideograph"><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">Please submit your article using
        the online manuscript submission service at </span><a
        href="https://mc.manuscriptcentral.com/cs-ieee"><b><span
            style="font-family:
            &quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">https://mc.manuscriptcentral.com/cs-ieee</span></b></a><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">. When uploading your article,
        select the appropriate special-issue title under the category
        &#8220;Manuscript
        Type.&#8221; Also include complete contact information for all
        authors. If you have
        any questions about submitting your article, contact the peer
        review
        coordinator at </span><a
href="javascript:location.href='mailto:'+String.fromCharCode(99,105,115,101,64,99,111,109,112,117,116,101,114,46,111,114,103)+'?'"><b><span
            style="font-family:&quot;Times New
            Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">cise@computer.org</span></b></a><span
        style="font-family:&quot;Times New
        Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;">.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
